{"name":"Question Mark Block","hex":"#ef9a49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"question","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A worded or expressed sentence, phrase, or only a word on its own, which asks for information, a reply, or a response; an interrogative.","A subject or topic for consideration or investigation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ask questions of; to interrogate; to ask for information.","To raise doubts about; have doubts about."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/question"},{"term":"mark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Boundary, land within a boundary.\n A boundary; a border or frontier. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n A boundary-post or fence. \nA stone or post used to indicate position and guide travellers. \n\n The line indicating an athlete's starting-point. \n A type of small region or principality. \n\n A common, or area of common land, especially among early Germanic peoples.","A boundary; a border or frontier. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put a mark on (something); to make (something) recognizable by a mark; to label or write on (something).","To leave a mark (often an undesirable or unwanted one) on (something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mark"},{"term":"block","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substantial, often approximately cuboid, piece of any substance.","A chopping block: a cuboid base for cutting or beheading."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fill or obstruct (something) so that it is not possible to pass.","To prevent (something or someone) from passing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/block"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mark Block","blocks":[{"text":"Mark Block is an American political strategist who worked as chief of staff and campaign manager for Herman Cain during his unsuccessful 2012 campaign for the Republican presidential nomination. Block has previously worked for Americans for Prosperity."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Block","wikidata":"Q6766762"},{"title":"Question mark","blocks":[{"text":"The question mark ? is a punctuation mark that indicates a question or interrogative clause or phrase in many languages."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Question_mark","wikidata":"Q11169"},{"title":"Question","blocks":[{"text":"A question is an utterance which serves as a request for information. Questions are sometimes distinguished from interrogatives, which are the grammatical forms, typically used to express them. Rhetorical questions, for instance, are interrogative in form but may not be considered bona fide questions, as they are not expected to be answered."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Question_in_a_question_in_a_question_in_a_question.gif/330px-Question_in_a_question_in_a_question_in_a_question.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Question","wikidata":"Q189756"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Btv1b6000718s.png/500px-Btv1b6000718s.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Btv1b6000718s.png/500px-Btv1b6000718s.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"8th century punctus interrogativus from the Godescalc Evangelistary. (BnF NAL 1203, f. 6v.)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABtv1b6000718s.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Punctus_interrogativus_from_Bern%2C_B%C3%BCrgerbibliothek_Cod._162%2C_f._15r.jpg/500px-Punctus_interrogativus_from_Bern%2C_B%C3%BCrgerbibliothek_Cod._162%2C_f._15r.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Punctus_i